BlowUpStrategy
**************

Description
===========

This is an optional argument for *note graph: graph,, and for the methods that
eventually call it. Currently, the possible values are "Eliminate" and
"Saturate", which indicate two different ways of computing the (closure of the)
graph of a rational map. The default choice is "Eliminate" and this is
generally preferable.

Functions with optional argument named BlowUpStrategy:
======================================================

  * "ChernSchwartzMacPherson(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"
  * "degreeMap(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"
  * "EulerCharacteristic(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"
  * "graph(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"
  * "inverseMap(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"
  * "isBirational(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"
  * "projectiveDegrees(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"
  * "SegreClass(...,BlowUpStrategy=>...)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note BlowUpStrategy: BlowUpStrategy, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

