Certify -- whether to ensure correctness of output
**************************************************

Description
===========

This option accepts a *note Boolean: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean, value, default
value false.

If turned on in the methods *note inverseMap: inverseMap, and *note
approximateInverseMap: approximateInverseMap,, then it will be checked whether
the maps in input and output are one the inverse of the other, throwing an
error if they are not. Actually, *note approximateInverseMap:
approximateInverseMap, will first try to fix the error of the approximation.
When turned on in the methods *note projectiveDegrees: projectiveDegrees,,
*note degreeMap: degreeMap,, *note isBirational: isBirational,, *note
isDominant: isDominant,, *note SegreClass: SegreClass,, *note
EulerCharacteristic: EulerCharacteristic, and *note ChernSchwartzMacPherson:
ChernSchwartzMacPherson,, it means whether to use a non-probabilistic
algorithm.

Functions with optional argument named Certify:
===============================================

  * "approximateInverseMap(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "ChernSchwartzMacPherson(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "degreeMap(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "EulerCharacteristic(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "exceptionalLocus(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "inverseMap(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "isBirational(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "isDominant(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "projectiveDegrees(...,Certify=>...)"
  * "SegreClass(...,Certify=>...)"

