EulerCharacteristic -- topological Euler characteristic of a (smooth) projective variety
****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        EulerCharacteristic I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal defining a
        smooth projective variety $X\subset\mathbb{P}^n$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note BlowUpStrategy: BlowUpStrategy, => ..., default value
        "Eliminate",
      * *note Certify: Certify, => ..., default value false, whether to ensure
        correctness of output
      * *note Verbose: inverseMap_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value true,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the topological Euler
        characteristics of $X$.

Description
===========

This is an application of the method *note SegreClass: SegreClass,. See also
the corresponding methods in the packages CSM-A (see
http://www.math.fsu.edu/~aluffi/CSM/CSM.html ), by P. Aluffi, and *note
CharacteristicClasses: (CharacteristicClasses)Top,, by M. Helmer and C. Jost.

In general, even if the input ideal defines a singular variety $X$, the
returned value equals the degree of the component of dimension 0 of the
Chern-Fulton class of $X$. The Euler characteristic of a singular variety can
be computed via the method *note ChernSchwartzMacPherson:
ChernSchwartzMacPherson,.

In the example below, we compute the Euler characteristic of
$\mathbb{G}(1,4)\subset\mathbb{P}^{9}$, using both a probabilistic and a
non-probabilistic approach.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = Grassmannian(1,4,CoefficientRing=>ZZ/190181);                       |
|                                                                             |
|                ZZ                                                           |
|o1 : Ideal of ------[p   ..p   , p   , p   , p   , p   , p   , p   , p   ,   |
|              190181  0,1   0,2   1,2   0,3   1,3   2,3   0,4   1,4   2,4    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|p   ]                                                                        |
| 3,4                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : time EulerCharacteristic I                                              |
| -- used 0.477733s (cpu); 0.278545s (thread); 0s (gc)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = 10                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : time EulerCharacteristic(I,Certify=>true)                               |
|Certify: output certified!                                                   |
| -- used 0.0147029s (cpu); 0.014266s (thread); 0s (gc)                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 10                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

No test is made to see if the projective variety is smooth.

See also
========

  * *note euler(ProjectiveVariety): (Varieties)euler_lpProjectiveVariety_rp, --
    topological Euler characteristic of a (smooth) projective variety
  * *note ChernSchwartzMacPherson: ChernSchwartzMacPherson, --
    Chern-Schwartz-MacPherson class of a projective scheme
  * *note SegreClass: SegreClass, -- Segre class of a closed subscheme of a
    projective variety

Ways to use EulerCharacteristic:
================================

  * "EulerCharacteristic(Ideal)"

