        forceInverseMap(Phi,Psi)
  * Inputs:
      * Phi, a *note rational map: RationalMap,
      * Psi, a *note rational map: RationalMap,
  * Outputs:
      * *note null: (Macaulay2Doc)null,

Description
===========

This method allows to inform the system that two maps are one the inverse of
the other without performing any computation. This is useful in particular if
you calculate the inverse map using your own method.

Caveat
======

If the declaration is false, nonsensical answers may result.

See also
========

  * *note isInverseMap(RationalMap,RationalMap):
    isInverseMap_lpRationalMap_cmRationalMap_rp, -- checks whether two rational
    maps are one the inverse of the other
  * *note inverse(RationalMap): inverse_lpRationalMap_rp, -- inverse of a
    birational map

Ways to use forceInverseMap:
============================

  * "forceInverseMap(RationalMap,RationalMap)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note forceInverseMap: forceInverseMap, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

