image(RationalMap,ZZ) -- closure of the image of a rational map
***************************************************************

  * Function: *note image: (Macaulay2Doc)image,
  * Usage: 
        image Phi 
        image(Phi,d)
  * Inputs:
      * Phi, a *note rational map: RationalMap,
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal defining the closure of
        the image of Phi, or its degree d homogeneous component if d is passed

Description
===========

This computation is done through the kernel of a ring map representing the
rational map. See *note kernel(RingMap): (Macaulay2Doc)kernel_lpRingMap_rp, and
*note kernel(RingMap,ZZ): kernel_lpRingMap_cmZZ_rp, for more details.

See also
========

  * kernel(RingMap,ZZ) (missing documentation)
  * *note kernel(RingMap): (Macaulay2Doc)kernel_lpRingMap_rp, -- kernel of a
    ringmap
  * *note image(RationalMap,String): image_lpRationalMap_cmString_rp, --
    closure of the image of a rational map using the F4 algorithm
    (experimental)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "image(RationalMap)"
  * *note image(RationalMap,ZZ): image_lpRationalMap_cmZZ_rp, -- closure of the
    image of a rational map
