inverse(RationalMap) -- inverse of a birational map
***************************************************

  * Function: *note inverse: (Macaulay2Doc)inverse,
  * Usage: 
        inverse phi
        inverse(phi,Certify=>b)
  * Inputs:
      * phi, a *note rational map: RationalMap,, which has to be birational,
        and b is a *note boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is, true
        or false (the default value is false)
  * Outputs:
      * a *note rational map: RationalMap,, the inverse map of phi

Description
===========

inverse(phi,Certify=>true) is the same as *note inverseMap:
inverseMap,(phi,Certify=>true,Verbose=>false), while
inverse(phi,Certify=>false) applies a middle ground approach between *note
inverseMap: inverseMap,(phi,Certify=>true) and *note inverseMap:
inverseMap,(phi,Certify=>false). The procedure for the latter is as follows: It
first computes the inverse map of phi using psi = *note inverseMap: inverseMap,
phi. Then it is checked that *note psi phi p: RationalMap _us_st, == p and
*note phi psi q: RationalMap _us_st, == q, where p,q are, respectively, a *note
random point: point, on the *note source: source_lpRationalMap_rp, and the
*note target: target_lpRationalMap_rp, of phi. Finally, if the tests pass, the
command *note forceInverseMap: forceInverseMap,(phi,psi) is invoked and psi is
returned.

