point(QuotientRing) -- pick a random rational point on a projective variety
***************************************************************************

  * Function: *note point: point,
  * Usage: 
        point R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, the homogeneous
        coordinate ring of a closed subscheme $X\subseteq\mathbb{P}^n$ over a
        finite ground field
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in R defining a point on
        $X$

Description
===========

This function is a variant of the *note randomKRationalPoint:
(Macaulay2Doc)randomKRationalPoint, function, which has been further improved
and extended in the package *note MultiprojectiveVarieties:
(MultiprojectiveVarieties)Top,, see *note point(MultiprojectiveVariety):
(MultiprojectiveVarieties)point_lpMultiprojectiveVariety_rp,.

Below we verify the birationality of a rational map.

