rationalMap(Ring,Tally) -- rational map defined by an effective divisor
***********************************************************************

  * Function: *note rationalMap: rationalMap,
  * Usage: 
        rationalMap D
        rationalMap(R,D)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the coordinate ring of a locally
        factorial projective variety $X\subseteq\mathbb{P}^n$
      * D, a *note tally: (Macaulay2Doc)Tally,, a multiset of homogeneous
        ideals in $R$ (or in *note ambient: (Macaulay2Doc)ambient, $R$)
        defining pure codimension 1 subschemes of $X$ with no embedded
        components; so that D is interpreted as an effective divisor on $X$
