SegreClass -- Segre class of a closed subscheme of a projective variety
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        SegreClass I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal of a
        graded quotient ring $K[x_0,\ldots,x_n]/J$ defining a subscheme
        $X=V(I)$ of $Y=Proj(K[x_0,\ldots,x_n]/J)\subseteq
        \mathbb{P}^n=Proj(K[x_0,\ldots,x_n])$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note BlowUpStrategy: BlowUpStrategy, => ..., default value
        "Eliminate",
      * *note Certify: Certify, => ..., default value false, whether to ensure
        correctness of output
      * *note Verbose: inverseMap_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value true,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the push-forward to
        the Chow ring of $\mathbb{P}^n$ of the Segre class $s(X,Y)$ of $X$ in
        $Y$

Description
===========

This is an example of application of the method *note projectiveDegrees:
projectiveDegrees,; see Proposition 4.4 in Intersection theory (see
http://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-3-662-02421-8 ), by W. Fulton, and
Subsection 2.3 in Lectures on Cremona transformations (see
http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/~idolga/cremonalect.pdf ), by I. Dolgachev. See
also the corresponding methods in the packages CSM-A (see
http://www.math.fsu.edu/~aluffi/CSM/CSM.html ), by P. Aluffi, and *note
CharacteristicClasses: (CharacteristicClasses)Top,, by M. Helmer and C. Jost.

In the example below, we take $Y\subset\mathbb{P}^7$ to be the dual
hypersurface of $\mathbb{P}^1\times\mathbb{P}^1\times\mathbb{P}^1\subset{\
mathbb{P}^7}^*$ and $X\subset Y$ its singular locus. We compute the
push-forward to the Chow ring of $\mathbb{P}^7$ of the Segre class both of $X$
in $Y$ and of $X$ in $\mathbb{P}^7$, using both a probabilistic and a
non-probabilistic approach.

