specialCremonaTransformation -- special Cremona transformations whose base locus has dimension at most three
************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        specialCremonaTransformation i 
        specialCremonaTransformation(i,K)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an integer between 1 and 12
      * K, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the ground field (optional, the
        default value is *note QQ: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,)
  * Outputs:
      * a *note rational map: RationalMap,, an example of special Cremona
        transformation over K, according to the classification given in Table 1
        of Special cubic Cremona transformations of P6 and P7 (see
        https://www.degruyter.com/view/journals/advg/19/2/article-p191.xml ).

Description
===========

A Cremona transformation is said to be special if the base locus scheme is
smooth and irreducible. To ensure this condition, the field K must be large
enough but no check is made.

